Subject: widgets: QFileDialog's tilde expansion without a passwd database

WHAT / WHY

  src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp
      Three hunks, all one cause: the wasi sysroot has no <pwd.h>.

      (a) The `#if defined(Q_OS_UNIX)` include block pulls in <pwd.h>
          unconditionally -- a hard "fatal error: 'pwd.h' file not found", and
          the ONLY thing that stopped QtWidgets compiling.
      (b) homeDirFromPasswdEntry() (getpwnam_r/getpwnam) is compiled out, so
          the file does not carry a static function nothing can call.
      (c) qt_tildeExpansion() takes the Q_OS_VXWORKS/Q_OS_INTEGRITY branch,
          which resolves "~" and "~/a/b" via QDir::homePath() and treats
          "~otheruser" as our own home rather than looking it up.

      (c) is the only behavioural change and it is the right one: a wasip2
      component has no user database to enumerate, so the only home directory
      that exists is its own.

UPSTREAM
  yes. Hunk (a) is a plain missing guard, and (b)/(c) reuse the escape hatch
  upstream already maintains for VxWorks and Integrity -- two other platforms
  with no passwd database. Nothing wk-specific.

---
diff --git a/src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp b/src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp
index ac2f288..13ebc96 100644
--- a/src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp
+++ b/src/widgets/dialogs/qfiledialog.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,9 @@
 #include <qstylepainter.h>
 #include "ui_qfiledialog.h"
 #if defined(Q_OS_UNIX)
-#include <pwd.h>
+#if !defined(Q_OS_WASI)
+#include <pwd.h>    // no user database, and no pwd.h, in the wasi sysroot
+#endif
 #include <unistd.h> // for pathconf() on OS X
 #elif defined(Q_OS_WIN)
 #  include <QtCore/qt_windows.h>
@@ -1122,6 +1124,7 @@ void QFileDialog::selectUrl(const QUrl &url)
 }
 
 #ifdef Q_OS_UNIX
+#ifndef Q_OS_WASI
 static QString homeDirFromPasswdEntry(const QString &path, const QByteArray &userName)
 {
 #if defined(_POSIX_THREAD_SAFE_FUNCTIONS) && !defined(Q_OS_OPENBSD) && !defined(Q_OS_WASM)
@@ -1147,6 +1150,7 @@ static QString homeDirFromPasswdEntry(const QString &path, const QByteArray &use
     return QFile::decodeName(pw->pw_dir);
 #endif // defined(_POSIX_THREAD_SAFE_FUNCTIONS) && !defined(Q_OS_OPENBSD) && !defined(Q_OS_WASM)
 }
+#endif // !Q_OS_WASI
 
 Q_AUTOTEST_EXPORT QString qt_tildeExpansion(const QString &path)
 {
@@ -1161,7 +1165,10 @@ Q_AUTOTEST_EXPORT QString qt_tildeExpansion(const QString &path)
     if (sepIndex == 1) // '~/' or '~/a/b/c'
         return QDir::homePath() + sv.sliced(1);
 
-#if defined(Q_OS_VXWORKS) || defined(Q_OS_INTEGRITY)
+// Q_OS_WASI joins these two for the same reason: there is no passwd database
+// to look "~otheruser" up in (and no <pwd.h> in the wasi sysroot), so the only
+// home directory that exists is our own.
+#if defined(Q_OS_VXWORKS) || defined(Q_OS_INTEGRITY) || defined(Q_OS_WASI)
     if (sepIndex == -1)
         return QDir::homePath();
     return QDir::homePath() + sv.sliced(sepIndex);
